WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.534
Joining us now, CNN military

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.003
analyst, retired Major General

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.970
James Spider

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.171
Marks and CNN

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.940
senior political commentator, former

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.042
Republican Congressman Adam Kinzinger.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.144
He's a lieutenant colonel in the U.S.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:14.014
Air National Guard. Spider, first to you.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.815
What do you make of the timeline

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:16.383
we're learning

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.685
now on when these German leopard tanks

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.820
will start arriving in Ukraine

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.022
and the fact that the U.S.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:22.655
will send

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.824
a more lethal, upgraded version

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.228
of the Abrams battle tanks?

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.263
Well, in my mind, it's all good news.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.798
But clearly, there's

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.899
a logistical tail

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.801
associated with the deployment

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.336
and then the training necessary

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.171
to get the Ukrainian forces up

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.373
to speed and confident with these

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.142
with these main battle tanks.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.109
Also, bear in mind,

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.311
you've got challengers from the U.K.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.447
So you have a mix of capabilities.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.581
You certainly have to address

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.949
the training the logistics,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.651
the maintenance, sustainment.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.319
But all those are considerations.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.922
Those aren't impediments or barriers

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.124
that would lead you to a decision,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.259
a no go decision

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.828
So I frankly am very glad

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.797
the United States has stepped forward.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.365
Germany has stepped forward.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.866
And all of those considerations

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.567
will be addressed.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.436
But there will be a time lag

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.104
between this decision

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.338
and when the realization

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.773
of all those capabilities

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.442
can be maximized on the battlefield.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.843
You're right, Adam.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.545
Ukraine is already pushing

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.814
we understand, for even more weapons.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.083
Very much on their wish list

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.751
include fighter jets.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.152
Do you see that as the next step

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.221
for Western allies potentially

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.157
Yeah, I think

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:31.524
what we

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.459
need to understand

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.593
here is pretty much

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.361
everything Ukraine is pushed for.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.896
It's taken a while for the U.S.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.431
and the allies to finally agree

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.166
that they, in fact, need that stuff.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:40.867
And part of

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.302
that is the United States

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.236
doesn't want to step out

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.370
too far ahead of Europe.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.573
It's keeping this alliance together.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.274
But I think the here's one of the biggest

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.309
untold things

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.543
that's going on in this war,

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.312
which is one of the struggles

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.580
in Eastern Europe over the past

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.615
decade or two, has been

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.584
they have old Russian equipment.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.219
How do they move over to NATO's

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.019
standard equipment?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.454
It's obviously very different supply

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.189
lines, very different training.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:03.723
And actually,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.825
what this war has done is flushed

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.527
a lot of that Russian equipment

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.662
in Eastern Europe into Ukraine.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.830
They've started bringing

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.332
a lot of these Eastern European countries

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.367
back into total, NATO's standard.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.135
And in Ukraine,

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.036
I think we have to look and recognize

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.438
Ukraine will be NATO's

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.206
standard military equipment country,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.941
and that includes F-16s.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.376
They have an excess capability

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.577
right now of pilots.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.712
I have talked to these pilots.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.546
I, in fact,

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.081
led the last effort in Congress

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.449
to begin training them

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.684
that can come here and learn the F-16.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.785
It'll take a couple of months

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:33.653
because it's a very different

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.021
mission set.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.756
And, of course, weapons system

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.024
that way they're ready

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.960
if and probably inevitably when the U.S.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.695
and the West decide to send F-16s

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.029
that way.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.497
Yeah, the Ukrainians have made it

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.499
abundantly clear they want the U.S.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.002
to start supplying F-16 fighter jets.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.004
Very important development potentially.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.205
Indeed, Spider,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.274
the fight is still incredibly intense

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.075
in the eastern part of Ukraine.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:56.676
But are U.S.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.677
officials right

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.344
to advise

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.712
Ukraine to cut its losses

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.415
there and prepare for renewed offensives?

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:04.584
Well, the

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.853
renewed offensive is going to come

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.755
And I would tell you that it will come.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:11.291
It will arrive in the Donbass area

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.326
or just north in the vicinity of Kharkiv,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.396
but will also be to bolster

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:16.963
the presence

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.998
that exists within the land bridge

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.134
and in the vicinity of Crimea.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.002
Clearly, an opportunity exists

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:23.970
for the Ukrainians

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.538
to try to separate

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.439
those forces

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.640
along the land bridge

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.409
in the direction of Crimea.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:30.743
Once you do that, you can

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.979
then hold the shoulder of one of those

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.547
and reduce the other.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.382
You can't do it all at once.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.452
That is the long term objective.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:42.622
But taking that peninsula of Crimea

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.824
is going to be very difficult.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.926
We're told Adam that President Biden

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.061
is considering a trip

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:48.528
to Europe,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.129
possibly Poland,

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.331
to mark the anniversary

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.433
in February of Putin's invasion.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.534
It'll be one year

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.236
next month if he takes that step.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.103
The president.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.005
What sort of message would hit send

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.073
if he went actually

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.941
went inside Ukraine itself?

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:04.611
Well, I think if he

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.245
win, it would send

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.713
a very powerful message.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.048
I think we can't necessarily be critical

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.682
if he doesn't.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:09.916
You know,

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.651
being the president of the United States

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.052
is even a

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.387
very different security threat

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.856
than any other really head of state.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.158
And that's a big deal and a big footprint

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.727
if he actually did pull that off.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.027
I'll tell you,

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.662
I think it would be massive.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.764
I think it would send chills in the

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.232
in the Russian leadership.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.634
I think it would embolden

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.602
the Ukrainian people because, look,

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.671
Ukraine has shown the will to fight.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.905
That's the one thing we have

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:33.606
seen as they have

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.841
absolutely shown,

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:35.742
that they are willing

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.610
to fight to defend freedom.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.112
You have somebody that's leading

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:39.612
the country

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.446
that leads freedom

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.948
even in times that we struggle

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.416
sometimes here

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.250
I think that sends

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.885
an extremely strong message

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.553
that we are in this.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.622
And the psychological impact of

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.923
just going there and saying

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.658
we're going to be with you

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.325
forever

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.726
is what can give Ukraine

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:54.894
the fighting spirit to go through

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:57.363
what is going to be a pretty tough,

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.531
pretty tough few months.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.400
Former Congressman Adam Kinzinger,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.301
thank you very much.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.802
Retired Major General Spider

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.203
Marks, thanks to you as well.

